What's this?

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.700
Who knows. It sounds creepy.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.000
Want a drink?

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:08.100
Any idea, Nanmo?

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.180
Huh?

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.680
Ow, hot!

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:37.840
Die!

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:49.990
Something huge was warping towards us.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.980
What was that thing?

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.310
Nanmo, trace it on the radar.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:57.830
Nothing?

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:01.130
That means it warped again,
right before it hit us.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.120
Even so, what was that?

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.090
And how did it?

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:22.240
Look, all I'm going to do is
take a shower and get dressed!

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:26.650
I'm just going to use the hotel shower! How
many times do I have to say it, you blockhead?!

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.290
No matter how many times you say it,
I'll only give you the same answer. Got it?

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:36.130
On our planet, people who arrive on
rental ships aren't allowed out of the spaceport.

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.830
That's the rule.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.400
I don't have time for this!
I'm going to be late!

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.670
I have to fly to Antares after this!

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:47.170
Are you telling me to go on a date
looking like I've been beat up?!

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.540
Not my problem.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.370
What?!

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:51.740
Ow!

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:53.680
Th-That's the rule!

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:54.080
Honestly.
Th-That's the rule!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:54.350
Honestly.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:54.820
Honestly.
Just forget about the rules for a second!

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.810
Just forget about the rules for a second!

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:57.820
Let go of him!

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:58.490
I'm not letting him go!
Let go of him!

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:00.060
I'm not letting him go!

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:01.850
Back... off!

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.590
My apologies.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.300
You mean, you're...

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.760
...the Dirty... Pair?

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:11.500
Lovely Angels!
Lovely Angels!

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.200
Understood! I'll make arrangements
with the hotel immediately!

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.600
P-Please don't kill me!

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.970
What are we, vicious criminals?

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:21.340
Can't you think a little before you act?!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.060
Die!

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.400
Kei!

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:31.850
What's that?!

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.620
Nanmo, standby for launch!

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.840
What's going on?!

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:11.610
Stay away!

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.730
It's deliberate...
They're missing me on purpose!

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:44.580
Ah... If you're leaving, you need to
go through the departure procedure.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:47.320
That's only if we went through
the arrival procedure, right?

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.360
U-Um...

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.760
It's the rule...

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.330
Here they come again!

00:08:56.330 --> 00:08:57.870
Nanmo, prepare the missiles!

00:08:57.870 --> 00:09:00.270
Ah! That's right, this ship...

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.360
It doesn't have any attack capabilities!

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.400
All I can do is run?!

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:18.290
Hey! Officer!

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.350
What happened, Miss?

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:23.690
I'm being chased by
something weird. It's over there.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:25.020
Something weird?

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:29.720
W-What is that?

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:31.330
I'm counting on you!

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:31.830
What?! You thief!
I'm counting on you!

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.730
What?! You thief!

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.020
So, you like me that much, huh?

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.010
In that case!

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:07.700
Ah?

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:08.960
Ow...

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:11.040
Kei! Grab on!

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:48.080
Why aren't they attacking?

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.340
Nanmo, stop the ship.

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:49.710
Why?
Nanmo, stop the ship.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.150
Why?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:50.410
Why?
They want to capture us alive, I'm sure of it.

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:54.020
They want to capture us alive, I'm sure of it.

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:57.710
They've already had several
chances to kill us, right?

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.400
So we wait for them to make their move?

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:09.630
Yeah.
So we wait for them to make their move?

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:10.330
Yeah.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:39.930
What?!

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:45.400
We're moving!

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.880
H-Hey, Yuri...

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:00.720
...I sure hope you're coming up
with a plan right now.

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:03.790
O-Of course I am. You are too, right?

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:05.340
O-Of course.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:12.690
Here it comes!
Here it comes!

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:16.830
It's that light again!

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:30.040
What's that?!

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.640
Th-This is!

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:38.940
It looks familiar.

00:12:42.220 --> 00:12:43.590
I-I think it's...

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:50.100
W-What is it?

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.830
Dammit, I can't remember.

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:09.380
Hey, do you think we should
let them take us inside like this?

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:12.550
You're the one who said we should
wait and see what happens.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:13.960
I did?

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:15.550
Nanmo, what do you think?

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:24.230
Now I remember!

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:29.770
This is the disposal station for radioactive waste,
poisonous organisms, and pollutants.

00:13:29.770 --> 00:13:32.070
Criados, "The Graveyard of Nothingness"!

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:37.450
But wasn't it closed down
due to a lot of crew accidents?

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:41.020
Looks like someone reopened it just for us.

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:47.180
Nanmo, dig up everyone associated with Criados
who might have a grudge against us.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:50.860
We need to come up with a plan, fast!

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:02.900
Hurry, hurry...

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.970
...or else I won't make it in time!

00:14:04.970 --> 00:14:08.340
He's already waiting for me
at table seven at Café Flamingo!

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:10.410
You're gonna keep saying that 'til you die!

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:10.650
Leave me alone!
You're gonna keep saying that 'til you die!

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:11.270
Leave me alone!

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.880
"J.S. Criados."

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.340
But he's dead.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:19.580
What's happening?!

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.750
Yuri, the spacesuits!

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:35.700
Nanmo, we're evacuating.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:01.600
I definitely don't like this
"wait and see what happens next" plan!

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.960
What else can we do in this situation?

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:07.420
Kei!

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.640
Kei!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:32.620
I owe you one, Nanmo.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.160
Kei!

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:41.660
Kei, can you hear me? Answer me!

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.440
You're alive, right?!

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:51.080
Kei, answer me!

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.180
Kei... Kei!

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:58.850
Oh wow, what a hunk!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:15:59.980
Huh? Where, where?

00:16:03.220 --> 00:16:05.520
Yep... So predictable!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.350
Nanmo! Give me all your
data on J.S. Criados.

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:16.860
"J.S. Criados was an authority on cerebral
physiology, cosmophysics, and astrobiology."

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:21.980
"He was also well versed in paranormal analysis,
synthetic biology, and psionic entities."

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:22.910
What the heck?

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.250
Quite impressive.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:26.480
So basically, he's a
scatterbrain that can't focus.

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:29.550
Oh! Do you remember
the Problintana mission?

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.050
The hallucinogenic drug?

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:34.890
That time when we destroyed the entire Problintana
distribution network, from the source to its dealers?

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:40.390
Right. Criados, the architect of this
disposal station, was a Problintana addict!

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.400
So he's a mad scientist, huh?

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:44.700
Just what we need, a weirdo with a grudge!

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:48.200
But he committed suicide
a year and a half ago.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:53.910
Are you saying he came back from
the dead and is trying kill us?

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:59.110
A brilliant genius like him could have
programmed any kind of trap before he died.

00:16:59.110 --> 00:17:01.820
So something that crazy is feasible, huh?

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:03.810
It's not out of the question.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:09.620
Even if that's the case, I don't have time to
play around with some dejected ghost!

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:11.890
Where's the main computer? I'll destroy it!

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.450
Yuri! Yuri, what's wrong?!

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:16.460
"Execution countdown"?

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:01.870
I... I'm stuck!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.810
Oh, great...

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:35.780
I told her we shouldn't
wait around to see what it'd do.

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:43.680
Hi, fancy meeting you here. You alive?

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:47.520
Yeah, no thanks to that ugly thing.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.330
W-What is that?

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:58.100
I'm sure it's something he made.

00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:00.970
Ten more minutes, and we'll be
up close and personal with it.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:12.440
Nanmo!

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:13.600
Nanmo!

00:19:17.720 --> 00:19:18.780
Nanmo...

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.460
What is it doing?

00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:39.770
What are we supposed to do with this?

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:47.910
What does this mean?

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.550
That's Nanmo's memory disk!

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:51.920
But why?

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.690
Die!

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:04.490
Die!

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:08.840
There's no way I'm gonna die!

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:11.700
He's still waiting for me
at table seven at Café Flamingo!

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:14.580
What did Nanmo want us to do with this?

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.710
Nanmo was made a year ago...

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:19.080
...but Criados died a year and a half ago.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:20.150
That's it!

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:23.780
Criados couldn't have known about Nanmo's
self-destruct mechanism when he made all this!

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.980
Yuri, take Nanmo's legs off!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:30.120
Hurry! That's what Nanmo wants us to do!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:39.000
To think Nanmo's Classified Information
Protection System would come in handy like this...

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:39.370
They're not coming off!
To think Nanmo's Classified Information
Protection System would come in handy like this...

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:40.170
They're not coming off!

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.360
Stick your finger through the opening
and push the round button!

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:49.980
They're off!

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:52.750
Face it towards that computer
and press the switches on both sides!

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:53.510
Huh?!

00:20:53.510 --> 00:20:57.180
As long as we have Nanmo's
memory disk, it can be rebuilt!

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:57.880
Hurry!

00:20:58.320 --> 00:20:59.410
Hurry!

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:07.320
Die!

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:46.630
Nanmo...

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:49.540
I can use this!

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:52.040
It's built for a pilot, even though
the computer was controlling it before.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:55.540
Since you have that disk, you can
start rebuilding Nanmo right away.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:56.810
Okay, see you later!

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:58.770
Hey, wait a minute!

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:01.850
I have a date, remember? See you!

00:22:01.850 --> 00:22:05.720
Table seven at Café Flamingo, here I come!

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:10.480
No spaceport is going to let you dock
such a contaminated ship, you know.

00:22:14.530 --> 00:22:19.360
You jerk!

00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:49.530
The mystery began after I fell asleep that time
Ano toki nemuri no ato ni okotta mistuerii

00:22:49.530 --> 00:22:56.140
I was guided by a voice from the future
Mirai kara kuru koe ni michibikareta no yo

00:22:56.140 --> 00:23:02.610
I passed through a distant, silvery time tunnel
Giniro haruka na taimu tonneru nukete

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:09.280
And met a wanderer with unclouded eyes
Deatta sunda me no samayoibito

00:23:09.550 --> 00:23:11.720
Space Fantasy

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:15.960
